    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.3.0

requires_dist unchanged. 0.3.0 newly claims /usr/bin/modelscope and
/usr/bin/ms, which python-modelscope 1.39.1 already owns and pulls in via
Requires - a hard file conflict. Both are removed in %install (bare rm,
so the build breaks loudly once upstream resolves script ownership).
133 tests pass.</comment>
    <requestid>1374589</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>64a4a5a1f00b1228a068feec98eaa914</srcmd5>
    <version>0.3.1</version>
    <time>1788361213</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.3.1

- Upload tunables renamed to canonical MODELSCOPE_UPLOAD_* names that spell out
  their unit; the old names still work but emit a FutureWarning.
- Folder upload caching now defaults to MODELSCOPE_UPLOAD_CACHE_ENABLED instead
  of a hardcoded True, for both the API and the CLI --use-cache flag.
- MCP servers listed via GET /mcp/servers, falling back to the legacy PUT and
  retrying anonymously when a stale or readonly token is rejected.
- Legacy AIGC create_model/create_model_tag take readme_content; create_model_tag
  reconciles a timed-out tag against the remote revision list.

Built locally on aarch64 and green on OBS x86_64 at srcmd5
64a4a5a1f00b1228a068feec98eaa914: 177 tests pass per Python flavour,
rpmlint 0 errors / 0 badness.</comment>
    <requestid>1375188</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="4" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>82978d15c480e87a1275b8ff37dd2031</srcmd5>
    <version>0.4.0</version>
    <time>1788518322</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.4.0

Follows 0.3.1 (SR 1375188), accepted into Factory earlier today.
Feature release with a credential-handling fix, not a version-string catch-up.

Fixes worth calling out:
- Legacy Studio compat stopped forwarding transport kwargs as business fields.
  update_studio_settings forwarded **kwargs as the settings payload, so a
  caller's API token could end up inside the PATCH request body and hence in
  server-side request logs; get_studio_logs(token=) raised TypeError, and
  per-call token=/endpoint= overrides were silently ignored. Factory's
  python-modelscope re-exports this class as modelscope.hub.api.HubApi, so the
  leak was reachable from a shipped Factory package.
- Studio create/update no longer silently drops cover_image (the outbound
  field rename ran the wrong way).
- Public Studio and MCP reads retry once anonymously, so a stale or read-scoped
  token can no longer hide data any anonymous caller can see.

Features:
- New Agent-IDP surface: Ed25519/JWK helpers, agent identity CRUD, key reset,
  pause, token issue and records, OIDC discovery and JWKS, as a new agent-idp
  subcommand. Private JWKs are written 0600 and only to an explicitly requested
  path. This is what pulls in the new cryptography &gt;= 41 dependency, added as
  both BuildRequires and Requires.
- Studio list, plaintext variables, hardware tiers, base images and SDK
  versions across the API, the CLI and the legacy compat layer; new
  StudioVisibility (adds a protected state the integer Visibility cannot
  express) and TokenScope enums; repo list gains --repo-type studio and
  mcp list gains --hosted.
- OpenAPI string error codes map to typed exceptions, including the new
  QuotaExceededError (E3027); signature, jwt and private_key added to the log
  redaction sets.

Consumer check: Factory's python-modelscope 1.39.1 imports 52 symbols from
modelscope_hub across 17 modules. All still resolve at runtime against the
built 0.4.0 RPM. compat/constants.py is byte-identical to 0.3.1 and
constants.py is purely additive, so no compat alias was dropped and no
constant changed value.

The rm of %{_bindir}/modelscope and %{_bindir}/ms in %install still applies:
upstream's pyproject still declares all four console scripts, the rm has no -f
and the build is green, and the RPMs ship only the -hub variants.

%check: the new tests/test_openapi_coverage.py needs tests/data/openapi.json,
which the sdist does not ship. The six tests taking that fixture are deselected;
the other 35 in that module (registry -&gt; method binding) still run.

Built locally on aarch64: 296 passed / 6 deselected per Python flavour (177 at
0.3.1), rpmlint 0 errors / 0 badness.</comment>
    <requestid>1375445</requestid>
  </revision>
